Project workflow:
- Before proposing a listing: `scripts/opportunity-report.sh`. I pick Teal or C# per session; don't choose for me.
- `tpr` is a blocking human watch loop - never run it; use `scripts/render-check.sh` (`-h` lists flags).
- Style fidelity matters: before writing a listing, read the 2 closest sibling templates (same data shape: list / table / log) and copy their palette, type scale, spacing and section structure. Read their render file in full; for a long style.css read the ranges you will reuse (e.g. `sed -n '/^h1 {/,/^}/p'`). Skip unrelated stylesheets.
- Never read `preview.html`, `output/**/*.html`, or the 300dpi PNG; use render-check numbers, and `read_image` crops when a visual check is genuinely needed.
- Mirror surrounding idioms (records, data binding, DOM structure) so generated code matches.
- After a new PDF listing, follow `listing_prompt.txt`.
- `teal/runtime.tl` selects the document; use unique 2-4 word slug folders so no existing folders in documents/ get overwritten; enable images for the final run.
